cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use msfc-ccd in your research, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: msfc-ccd
abstract: >-
  msfc-ccd is a Python library for characterizing and using the CCD cameras
  built by NASA Marshall Space Flight Center (MSFC) for solar instruments
  flown on sounding rockets, such as the EUV Snapshot Imaging Spectrograph
  (ESIS). It reads the FITS files that the cameras produce, models the camera
  and its Teledyne/e2v CCD230-42 sensor, and turns a raw readout into a
  calibrated image by splitting it into the four taps of the sensor, removing
  the bias measured from the blank columns, and converting to electrons. The
  library also measures the properties of each tap from calibration
  exposures: readout noise from sequences of darks, dark current from darks
  of several exposure lengths, gain from the photon transfer of flats and
  from Fe 55 X-ray events, and charge transfer efficiency from the extended
  pixel edge response of flats and from Fe 55 events. It is built on
  named-arrays, so images and sequences of images carry named axes and
  physical units.
